{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "The library will be implemented in Go, consistent with Hyperledger Fabric's primary language.",
    "The implementation will follow the existing patterns and conventions used in Fabric's channel configuration code (e.g., `common/configtx` and related packages).",
    "For capabilities management (U5), the design will use discrete enable/disable functions for each capability version (e.g., `EnableV2_0ApplicationCapabilities`), rather than allowing arbitrary capability strings. This ensures type safety and prevents misconfiguration.",
    "New helper functions will operate on the `*common.ConfigGroup` and `*common.Config` types directly, providing low-level, reusable tools.",
    "For configuration retrieval functions (U3, U4, U6), the functions will return the strongly-typed Fabric protobuf message types (e.g., `*common.Capabilities`, `*common.Application`).",
    "The example tests (U8) will be separate, focused test files or functions within the existing test suite, each demonstrating a specific configuration scenario."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The developer has intermediate-to-advanced familiarity with the Hyperledger Fabric codebase, specifically the channel configuration protobuf structures and the `configtx` tool/library.",
    "The existing codebase has a functioning test infrastructure (unit tests, integration tests, example tests) that will be reused.",
    "The 'example test' mentioned in the spec is a Go test file (e.g., `*_test.go`) that serves as both documentation and executable verification.",
    "No changes to the underlying protobuf definitions (`common/configtx.proto`) are required; all functions work with the existing message structures.",
    "The 'signature workflow' mentioned in U1/U2 acceptance criteria is an existing process within the library or Fabric CLI; the library's responsibility ends with generating the `ConfigUpdate` transaction envelope, ready for signing.",
    "The 'orderer org's config group' is identified by its group key within the channel configuration (e.g., 'OrdererOrgs' under the 'Orderer' section)."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement Orderer Endpoint Management",
      "activity_description": "Implement the two core functions for U1 and U2: `AddOrdererEndpoint(config *common.Config, ordererOrgGroup string, endpoint string)` and `RemoveOrdererEndpoint(config *common.Config, ordererOrgGroup string, endpoint string)`. Each function will modify the in-memory `*common.Config` and return an updated config ready for generating a `ConfigUpdate`.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Policy Retrieval Helper",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function for U3: `GetPoliciesForOrg(config *common.Config, orgType OrgType, orgName string)` (where `OrgType` is an enum for Application/Orderer/Consortium). This will parse the config tree and return the `*common.Policies` map for the specified organization.",
      "most_likely_effort": 12
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement Capabilities Retrieval",
      "activity_description": "Implement the three functions for U4: `GetOrdererCapabilities(config *common.Config)`, `GetApplicationCapabilities(config *common.Config)`, and `GetChannelCapabilities(config *common.Config)`. Each will return the corresponding `*common.Capabilities`.",
      "most_likely_effort": 10
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement Capabilities Modification",
      "activity_description": "Implement the discrete enable/disable functions for U5 (e.g., `EnableOrdererV2_0Capabilities(config *common.Config)`, `DisableApplicationV1_3Capabilities(config *common.Config)`, etc.). This includes handling all three capability sets (Orderer, Application, Channel). The logic involves finding the appropriate `Capabilities` message in the config and toggling the boolean flags.",
      "most_likely_effort": 18
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement Application Config Retrieval",
      "activity_description": "Implement the function for U6: `GetApplicationConfig(config *common.Config)`. This will traverse the config to find and return the `*common.Application` group, which contains policies, ACLs, capabilities, etc.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement ACL Management",
      "activity_description": "Implement the functions for U7: `AddACL(config *common.Config, aclKey string, aclValue *common.ACL)` and `RemoveACL(config *common.Config, aclKey string)`. These will modify the `ACLs` map within the `Application` group of the config.",
      "most_likely_effort": 14
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Write Unit Tests for Core Functions",
      "activity_description": "Develop unit tests for all functions implemented in A1-A6. Tests will cover happy paths, edge cases (e.g., org not found, duplicate endpoint), and verification that the config is mutated correctly.",
      "most_likely_effort": 30
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Create Focused Example Tests (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Refactor and extend the existing example test. Create separate, focused test/example functions as per U8 acceptance: (1) Updating Orderer Configuration, (2) Updating Application Configuration, (3) Organization Management (covers U1/U2), (4) MSP Modifications (likely demonstrating retrieval via U3/U6), (5) Capabilities Management (covers U4/U5).",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Integration and API Validation",
      "activity_description": "Perform a final round of integration testing within the test suite, ensuring the new functions work correctly together in the context of building a full configuration update transaction and that the overall API is consistent and intuitive.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 156
  }
}
```

